# Temugank Architecture

Follow the four-layer structure. Full docs: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`.

## Layers

```
config/ + content/     →  what (data)
lib/ + types/          →  logic (no UI)
pages/ + layouts/      →  routes (thin orchestrators)
components/            →  UI (astro = static, islands = React)
```

## Folder rules

| Path | Contains |
|------|----------|
| `src/config/` | Site constants: nav, brand, section IDs |
| `src/content/` | JSON content entries |
| `src/lib/content/` | `getHomePageData()` and page loaders |
| `src/lib/motion/` | Framer variants, transitions, reduced-motion hook |
| `src/lib/cn.ts` | className helper |
| `src/components/astro/` | Zero-JS `.astro` components |
| `src/components/islands/` | React components (require `client:*`) |
| `src/components/ui/` | Shared presentational React primitives |

## When editing code

- Pages fetch content via `lib/content/` helpers — not inline `getCollection()` maps
- Islands receive data as props — no content fetching inside React
- Prefer `.astro` over React; use islands only for interactivity or motion
- Editable copy goes in `content/` or `config/`, never hardcoded in components
- Use `@/` import alias for all src imports

## Hydration

- `client:load` — header, hero (above the fold)
- `client:visible` — animated sections below the fold
- Never import a React island without a `client:*` directive

